Building the Zabbix proxy on Windows
====================================

The proxy is 64-bit only and links a database engine and an event loop that the
agent does not need. It is therefore not part of the default `nmake all` target;
build it explicitly.

Scope of this build
-------------------

Active and passive proxy, SQLite3 buffer, Zabbix agent checks, simple checks,
trapper, preprocessing (including JavaScript), data sender and housekeeper.

Not included: SNMP, IPMI, VMware, ODBC database monitor and ICMP ping. The
corresponding sources are still compiled and linked, but their internal HAVE_*
guards leave them reporting the check as unsupported.

Prerequisites
-------------

  * Visual Studio Build Tools with the C++ toolset and a Windows SDK
  * vcpkg, used with the `x64-windows-static` triplet so the result matches the
    /MT runtime the Zabbix Windows build uses

Install the third-party libraries from the manifest in this directory:

    vcpkg install --triplet x64-windows-static

That provides zlib, OpenSSL, PCRE2, libevent, SQLite3 and libcurl.

Building from a git checkout
----------------------------

Two files the release tooling produces are absent from a git tree, and both are
needed here:

  * src/libs/zbxdbschema/dbschema.c, generated by

        perl create/bin/gen_schema.pl c > src/libs/zbxdbschema/dbschema.c

  * the version stamps in include/version.h, which still read {ZABBIX_REVISION}
    and {ZABBIX_RC_NUM}. Pass ZBX_REVISION and ZBX_RC_NUM to nmake; they default
    to 0 so that the version resource at least compiles.

Neither is specific to the proxy - any Windows target built from git needs them.

Building
--------

From a "x64 Native Tools Command Prompt", in build\win32\project:

    set VCPKG=<vcpkg root>\installed\x64-windows-static

    nmake /f Makefile_proxy ^
        TLS=openssl ^
        TLSINCDIR=%VCPKG%\include TLSLIBDIR=%VCPKG%\lib ^
        PCRE2INCDIR=%VCPKG%\include PCRE2LIBDIR=%VCPKG%\lib ^
        SQLITE3INCDIR=%VCPKG%\include SQLITE3LIBDIR=%VCPKG%\lib ^
        LIBEVENTINCDIR=%VCPKG%\include LIBEVENTLIBDIR=%VCPKG%\lib ^
        CURLINCDIR=%VCPKG%\include CURLLIBDIR=%VCPKG%\lib ^
        ZLIBINCDIR=%VCPKG%\include ZLIBLIBDIR=%VCPKG%\lib

The binary is written to bin\win64\zabbix_proxy.exe.

Notes
-----

The proxy build selects build\win32\include\proxy\config.h ahead of the agent's
config.h through ADD_INCS; both files are named config.h on purpose, so that the
platform-independent sources include the right one without modification.

Linking goes through a response file because the proxy links over 350 objects,
which does not fit on a command line.
